# Stale dependencies we have looked at and decided to keep. Each entry is on
# its latest available version, so there is nothing to upgrade to. Re-check any
# decision older than a year rather than trusting it.
#
# modrot matches the module path alone, so a reason has to sit on its own '#'
# line above the entry. An inline comment stops the entry from matching at all.

# 2026-09-30 keep: latest commit, niche setproctitle binding with no successor
github.com/ErikDubbelboer/gspt

# 2026-09-30 keep: latest commit, James Hunt's own libraries, which shield was
# written around. 41 files import go-ansi and 14 import go-table, so replacing
# either is a port rather than a dependency bump.
github.com/jhunt/go-ansi

# 2026-09-30 keep: latest commit, 2 call sites, no successor
github.com/jhunt/go-envirotron

# 2026-09-30 keep: latest commit, see the go-ansi note above
github.com/jhunt/go-table

# 2026-09-30 keep: latest tag v1.2.1. github.com/google/uuid is the maintained
# successor and is already in the tree indirectly, but its Parse returns
# (UUID, error) where pborman's returns a nil UUID, so swapping it across 14
# files changes error handling rather than just an import path.
github.com/pborman/uuid

# 2026-09-30 keep: latest tag v1.0.6, 1 call site, no successor
github.com/thanhpk/randstr
